  "section_notes": "S2 keeps the 5% permanent limit and numeric customer disclosure but defers enforcement for five years with no interim cap, which mainly protects Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%). S5 mandates recall above 8 per 100,000 with no transition, which directly exposes Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9). S1 requires 24-hour reporting of all thermal incidents, closing the unreported-incident gap for both companies."
